Square QS tiles in the 2025 shade — the only real fix (SystemUI code, not an RRO).

The shade tiles are drawn by Compose with compile-time Dp radii; no resource feeds
them. Change these three constants and rebuild SystemUI:

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/panels/ui/compose/infinitegrid/CommonTile.kt
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/panels/ui/compose/infinitegrid/CommonTile.kt
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@ object CommonTileDefaults {
     val TileEndPadding = 12.dp
     val TileDualTargetEndPadding = 8.dp
     val TileArrangementPadding = 6.dp
-    val InactiveCornerRadius = 50.dp
+    val InactiveCornerRadius = 0.dp
     val TileLabelBlurWidth = 32.dp
     const val TILE_MARQUEE_ITERATIONS = 1
     const val TILE_INITIAL_DELAY_MILLIS = 2000
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/panels/ui/compose/infinitegrid/Tile.kt
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/panels/ui/compose/infinitegrid/Tile.kt
@@ -479,8 +479,8 @@ private object TileDefaults {
     val ActiveIconCornerRadius = 16.dp
-    val ActiveTileCornerRadius = 24.dp
+    val ActiveIconCornerRadius = 0.dp
+    val ActiveTileCornerRadius = 0.dp

(optional, edit mode) EditTile.kt:340 uses RoundedCornerShape(26.dp); EditTile.kt:695/828/833
use EditModeTileDefaults.GridBackgroundCornerRadius.

Verification after flashing the rebuilt SystemUI: the same measurement script
(evidence/qs-square/forensics/measure-shade.py) must report r ~= 0 for both the
inactive and the active tile; today it reports 35.5 dp and 23.7 dp.

Risk: rebuilding and replacing SystemUI is a much heavier and riskier change than an
RRO (platform signature / privapp permissions); it is not attempted here.
